      "A lot is the smallest quantity of incoming material you can treat as one population for inspection: same part number, revision, supplier, manufacturing lot or date code, packaging and process route. Mixed revisions, date codes or supplier plants are separate lots unless your quality plan says the differences cannot affect the characteristics being inspected. For SMT and THT material, a lot may be a reel, a tray stack, a bag of through-hole parts or a shipment of bare boards, depending on how the supplier controls traceability."
